id: pm-rust-admission-schema
title: Extend native admission to custom schemas and complex lifecycle intents
description: "The first admission contract explicitly refuses custom field/type schemas and terminal, blocked, dependency-sensitive or alias status transitions."
type: Task
status: open
priority: 3
tags[3]: admission,follow-up,native
created_at: "2026-10-29T04:40:13.941Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-29T07:15:13.932Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Extend shared native apply preparation before broadening preview admission; prove admitted/refused parity against the pinned published oracle for every newly declared schema and lifecycle slice.
parent: pm-rust-u4al
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-29T07:15:13.932Z",codex-agent,"Admission review class audit found that pinned pm CLI 2026.10.21 previewItemMutations admits a status-only update to the configured close status when its role is active, although create to the same target requires a close reason. Native scalar closure updates now refuse and remain outside the declared parity slice; retain this discrepancy when expanding lifecycle support. No upstream issue filed under task rules."
body: "Keep the preview and native write path on the same exported preparation functions. Preserve legacy data, explicit scope assertions, role-based status semantics and bounded source/output receipts. This is independent Rust implementation work, not an unavailable TypeScript SDK capability: the published previewItemMutations oracle already supplies the reference semantics."
